---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { UI } from '../lib/i18n';

const t = UI.en;
const GH = 'https://github.com/alv67/peculium';
---

<Base
  locale="en"
  path="/install"
  title={`${t.navLabel.install} · Peculium`}
  description="Install Peculium on your homelab: pull the public GHCR images and bring the whole stack up with one command."
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-16">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-extrabold tracking-tight">{t.navLabel.install}</h1>
    <p class="mt-4 text-lg leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300">
      Peculium is a classic self-hosted app, and installing it is pull-only: nothing is ever built
      on your machine. The official images are public on GitHub Container Registry — anonymous pulls,
      no login, no token — for <span class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-slate-100">linux/amd64</span>
      and <span class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-slate-100">linux/arm64</span>.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-xl font-bold">Prerequisites</h2>
    <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-2 pl-6 text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300">
      <li>
        <span class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-slate-100">Podman</span> (or Docker) with
        Compose support, on any Linux box, NAS or VM.
      </li>
      <li>
        A machine on <span class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-slate-100">amd64</span> or
        <span class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-slate-100">arm64</span> — the images are multi-arch.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400">
      The images are published on <code class="rounded bg-slate-100 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-xs dark:bg-slate-800">ghcr.io/alv67/peculium-*</code>
      (frontend, backend, worker, python-service, secrets-init) starting with the
      <span class="font-semibold">v1.0.0</span> release.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-xl font-bold">Step 1 — Download the stack files</h2>
    <p class="mt-2 text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300">Grab the release compose file and the environment template:</p>
    <pre class="mt-3 overflow-x-auto rounded-lg bg-slate-900 p-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-100"><code>curl -O https://raw.githubusercontent.com/alv67/peculium/main/docker-compose.yml
curl -O https://raw.githubusercontent.com/alv67/peculium/main/.env.example
cp .env.example .env   # optional</code></pre>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-xl font-bold">Step 2 — Configure (optional)</h2>
    <p class="mt-2 text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300">
      Everything has sensible defaults: you can skip <code class="rounded bg-slate-100 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-xs dark:bg-slate-800">.env</code>
      entirely and the stack boots with auto-generated secrets. Edit it only if you want to change
      something:
    </p>
    <div class="mt-4 overflow-x-auto">
      <table class="w-full border-collapse text-left text-sm">
        <thead>
          <tr class="border-b border-slate-200 text-xs uppercase tracking-wide text-slate-500 dark:border-slate-700 dark:text-slate-400">
            <th class="py-2 pr-4 font-semibold">Key</th>
            <th class="py-2 pr-4 font-semibold">Default</th>
            <th class="py-2 font-semibold">Notes</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody class="text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300">
          <tr class="border-b border-slate-100 dark:border-slate-800">
            <td class="py-2 pr-4 font-mono text-xs">PECULIUM_VERSION</td>
            <td class="py-2 pr-4 font-mono text-xs">latest</td>
            <td class="py-2">Image tag for every Peculium service — pin a release (e.g. <code class="font-mono text-xs">v1.0.0</code>) to keep the stack on a fixed version.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr class="border-b border-slate-100 dark:border-slate-800">
            <td class="py-2 pr-4 font-mono text-xs">PECULIUM_HTTP_PORT</td>
            <td class="py-2 pr-4 font-mono text-xs">3000</td>
            <td class="py-2">Host port the web UI is published on.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr class="border-b border-slate-100 dark:border-slate-800">
            <td class="py-2 pr-4 font-mono text-xs">POSTGRES_PASSWORD</td>
            <td class="py-2 pr-4 font-mono text-xs">(empty)</td>
            <td class="py-2">Leave empty to auto-generate a random one on first boot.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="py-2 pr-4 font-mono text-xs">PECULIUM_JWT_SECRET</td>
            <td class="py-2 pr-4 font-mono text-xs">(empty)</td>
            <td class="py-2">Leave empty to auto-generate a random one on first boot. Changing it logs everyone out.</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-xl font-bold">Step 3 — Start</h2>
    <pre class="mt-3 overflow-x-auto rounded-lg bg-slate-900 p-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-100"><code>podman-compose up -d</code></pre>
    <p class="mt-2 text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300">
      Web UI, API, worker, price service, PostgreSQL and Redis come up together; the first
      <code class="rounded bg-slate-100 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-xs dark:bg-slate-800">up</code>
      also generates and stores your secrets (see notes below).
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-xl font-bold">Step 4 — Open Peculium</h2>
    <p class="mt-2 text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300">
      Point your browser to <a href="http://localhost:3000" class="font-semibold text-brand hover:underline dark:text-brand-dark">http://localhost:3000</a>
      and create the first account. From there, add assets and portfolios and let Peculium pull quotes.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-xl font-bold">Good to know</h2>
    <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-2 pl-6 text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300">
      <li>
        <span class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-slate-100">Back up the secrets volume.</span>
        On first boot the database password and the JWT secret are auto-generated and persisted in
        the <code class="rounded bg-slate-100 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-xs dark:bg-slate-800">peculium_secrets</code>
        volume, then reused on every restart — if you lose that volume you lose access to the
        database.
      </li>
      <li>
        PostgreSQL and Redis are <span class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-slate-100">not</span>
        exposed on the host; only the web UI port is published (the backend is reachable through the
        frontend's <code class="rounded bg-slate-100 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-xs dark:bg-slate-800">/api/</code> proxy).
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-slate-100">To update</span>, pull the new
        tag and restart in place:
        <code class="rounded bg-slate-100 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-xs dark:bg-slate-800">PECULIUM_VERSION=vX.Y.Z podman-compose pull &amp;&amp; podman-compose up -d</code>
      </li>
    </ul>

    <p class="mt-10 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400">
      Something not working? Open an issue on{' '}
      <a href={`${GH}/issues`} rel="noopener" class="font-semibold text-brand hover:underline dark:text-brand-dark">GitHub</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
